WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.192 --> 00:00:16.396
The first month at Redmond College had seemed long, but the rest of the term went by quickly.

2
00:00:17.476 --> 00:00:22.718
Before they realized how much time had gone by, Anne and all the Redmond students were facing their

3
00:00:22.778 --> 00:00:30.120
exams. When the results came back, the top places in first-year subjects were taken by Anne, Gilbert, and

4
00:00:30.200 --> 00:00:35.456
Philippa. Priscilla did very well, and Charlie scraped through respectably.

5
00:00:36.877 --> 00:00:38.558
After exams, came vacation.

6
00:00:38.578 --> 00:00:45.024
"I can't believe that this time tomorrow I'll be in Green Gables," said Anne to Philippa on the

7
00:00:45.084 --> 00:00:46.245
night before her departure.

8
00:00:46.265 --> 00:00:48.067
"But I shall be.

9
00:00:48.567 --> 00:00:52.050
And you, Phil, will be in Bolingbroke with Alec and Alonzo."

10
00:00:52.070 --> 00:00:56.194
"I'm longing to see them," admitted Philippa.

11
00:00:56.214 --> 00:00:58.656
"They really are such nice boys.

12
00:00:59.624 --> 00:01:03.206
And in Bolingbroke there'll be dances and parties and all kinds of fun.

13
00:01:05.167 --> 00:01:09.328
But I shall never forgive you, Queen Anne, for not coming home with me for the holidays."

14
00:01:09.348 --> 00:01:11.769
"I'm sure you'll forgive me.

15
00:01:11.789 --> 00:01:15.311
'Never' lasts only three days with you, Phil!"

16
00:01:15.711 --> 00:01:16.371
joked Anne.

17
00:01:16.391 --> 00:01:21.274
"It was sweet of you to ask me and I'd love to go to Bolingbroke someday.

18
00:01:21.294 --> 00:01:26.216
I'd especially like to see the house where my parents lived and where I was born.

19
00:01:27.212 --> 00:01:30.254
But these holidays I must visit Green Gables."

20
00:01:30.274 --> 00:01:35.938
"You won't have a very good time," said Phil scornfully.

21
00:01:35.958 --> 00:01:38.520
"It sounds so boring there!"

22
00:01:38.540 --> 00:01:40.461
"In Avonlea?"

23
00:01:40.941 --> 00:01:42.502
said Anne, highly amused.

24
00:01:42.522 --> 00:01:48.566
"If you'd come with me to Bolingbroke," Phil insisted, "you'd have a wonderful time.

25
00:01:49.487 --> 00:01:54.590
People would go wild over you, Anne—your hair and your style and, oh, everything!

26
00:01:55.631 --> 00:01:56.532
You're so unique."

27
00:01:58.680 --> 00:02:02.802
"That sounds interesting, Phil, but picture this," Anne said.

28
00:02:02.822 --> 00:02:11.686
"I'm going home to an old country farmhouse, once green, rather faded now, set among some apple orchards.

29
00:02:12.686 --> 00:02:17.368
There's a stream nearby, and down the road is a wood with old fir trees.

30
00:02:18.489 --> 00:02:25.192
In the farmhouse there will be two middle-aged ladies: one tall and thin, one short and fat.

31
00:02:26.760 --> 00:02:28.161
They are Marilla and Mrs.

32
00:02:28.261 --> 00:02:35.105
Lynde. And there will be the twins, Dora and Davy—one a perfect model, the other what Mrs.

33
00:02:35.185 --> 00:02:36.485
Lynde calls a 'terror.'

34
00:02:37.686 --> 00:02:42.549
There will be a little room upstairs with an old feather bed, which will seem like heaven after

35
00:02:42.629 --> 00:02:45.130
sleeping on that hard mattress in the boardinghouse.

36
00:02:46.150 --> 00:02:47.611
How do you like my picture, Phil?"

37
00:02:47.631 --> 00:02:52.454
"It seems a very dull one," said Phil with a frown.

38
00:02:52.474 --> 00:02:58.021
"Oh, but I've left out one thing," said Anne softly.

39
00:02:58.041 --> 00:03:05.887
"There'll be love there, Phil—love like nowhere else in the world, tender love that's waiting for me.

40
00:03:06.747 --> 00:03:11.951
That makes my picture a masterpiece, doesn't it, even if the colors are not very bright?"

41
00:03:13.292 --> 00:03:15.974
Phil got up, went up to Anne, and hugged her.

42
00:03:15.994 --> 00:03:20.597
"Anne, I wish I were like you," she said soberly.

43
00:03:21.718 --> 00:03:24.980
The following evening Diana met Anne at the Avonlea station.

44
00:03:25.980 --> 00:03:30.681
As they drove up the lane, Anne saw that Green Gables had a very festive appearance.

45
00:03:31.802 --> 00:03:37.443
A candle burned in every window, and in the yard was a big bonfire with two little figures,

46
00:03:37.743 --> 00:03:39.884
Davy and Dora, dancing around it.

47
00:03:41.564 --> 00:03:45.625
"Davy was determined to make a bonfire for you," Diana told Anne.

48
00:03:46.846 --> 00:03:49.586
Anne got out of the buggy, and Davy hugged her tightly.

49
00:03:50.647 --> 00:03:52.007
Even Dora held her hand.

50
00:03:52.027 --> 00:03:54.668
"Isn't it a great bonfire, Anne?"

51
00:03:55.068 --> 00:03:56.716
asked Davy.

52
00:03:56.736 --> 00:03:58.297
"I'll poke it—see the sparks?

53
00:03:58.817 --> 00:04:01.698
I did it for you because I was so glad you were coming home."

54
00:04:04.019 --> 00:04:06.720
The kitchen door opened and Marilla greeted Anne.

55
00:04:07.681 --> 00:04:13.243
Marilla had a big smile, but not too big, since she had the old-fashioned belief that you should

56
00:04:13.283 --> 00:04:14.664
not show too much emotion.

57
00:04:15.684 --> 00:04:18.225
Mrs. Lynde was behind her, smiling warmly.

58
00:04:19.266 --> 00:04:21.526
They both hugged Anne and welcomed her home.

59
00:04:22.527 --> 00:04:24.788
This was the love Anne had described to Phil.

60
00:04:26.364 --> 00:04:29.906
A few days later, Anne met her old friend Jane Andrews.

61
00:04:30.886 --> 00:04:34.228
After they had caught up on each other's news, Jane grew silent.

62
00:04:35.008 --> 00:04:36.208
Then she turned to Anne.

63
00:04:36.228 --> 00:04:40.090
"I want to ask you something, Anne," she said solemnly.

64
00:04:40.110 --> 00:04:43.071
"What do you think of my brother Billy?"

65
00:04:44.012 --> 00:04:46.193
Anne gasped at this unexpected question.

66
00:04:47.033 --> 00:04:49.514
Goodness, what did she think of Billy Andrews?

67
00:04:51.335 --> 00:04:53.076
Anne had never thought anything about him.

68
00:04:53.896 --> 00:04:59.660
He was just the round-faced, perpetually smiling, not too smart, good-natured Billy Andrews.

69
00:04:59.680 --> 00:05:03.843
"I—I don't understand, Jane," Anne stammered.

70
00:05:03.863 --> 00:05:06.685
"What do you mean exactly?"

71
00:05:06.705 --> 00:05:08.447
"Do you like Billy?"

72
00:05:08.867 --> 00:05:09.848
asked Jane bluntly.

73
00:05:09.868 --> 00:05:15.552
"Oh, uh—yes, I like him, of course," said Anne.

74
00:05:16.472 --> 00:05:18.494
Anne knew that she didn't dislike him.

75
00:05:19.355 --> 00:05:21.076
What exactly was Jane trying to say?

76
00:05:23.348 --> 00:05:25.469
"Would you like him for a husband?"

77
00:05:25.889 --> 00:05:26.950
asked Jane calmly.

78
00:05:26.970 --> 00:05:28.771
"A husband!"

79
00:05:29.171 --> 00:05:29.871
Anne exclaimed.

80
00:05:29.891 --> 00:05:33.373
"Billy wants to marry you," Jane explained.

81
00:05:33.393 --> 00:05:36.474
"He's always been crazy about you.

82
00:05:37.514 --> 00:05:40.996
But he was too shy to ask you himself, so he got me to do it.

83
00:05:41.936 --> 00:05:43.877
I didn't want to ask you, but he insisted.

84
00:05:44.978 --> 00:05:46.519
Well, what do you think, Anne?"

85
00:05:48.519 --> 00:05:49.300
Was it a dream?

86
00:05:50.204 --> 00:05:54.968
Anne did not know whether she wanted to laugh or cry, but she could do neither, because she

87
00:05:55.008 --> 00:05:56.729
didn't want to hurt Jane's feelings.

88
00:05:57.970 --> 00:06:01.572
"I—I can't marry your brother, Jane," Anne said.

89
00:06:01.592 --> 00:06:05.495
"It never even occurred to me that Billy would ask!"

90
00:06:06.575 --> 00:06:09.017
"Well, think it over, Anne," said Jane.

91
00:06:09.037 --> 00:06:10.818
"Billy is a good fellow."

92
00:06:10.838 --> 00:06:15.722
"I'm sorry, I can't marry Billy," said Anne firmly.

93
00:06:15.742 --> 00:06:20.909
"Well, you've made your decision, Anne," replied Jane somewhat coldly.

94
00:06:20.929 --> 00:06:22.770
"And I hope you won't regret it.

95
00:06:23.670 --> 00:06:26.092
Billy is a good fellow, even if he is my brother.

96
00:06:27.072 --> 00:06:30.374
Anyway, he also likes Nettie Blewett, so he'll probably ask her."

97
00:06:30.394 --> 00:06:32.575
"Nettie Blewett!"

98
00:06:33.015 --> 00:06:33.576
Anne thought.

99
00:06:34.676 --> 00:06:38.699
After Jane had gone, Anne laughed but she also felt a hint of sadness.

100
00:06:40.540 --> 00:06:46.062
Anne had imagined that her first proposal would be very romantic, and that it would come from someone

101
00:06:46.103 --> 00:06:50.177
who was handsome, distinguished, and eloquent—her own Prince Charming.

102
00:06:51.198 --> 00:06:53.200
There was nothing romantic about this proposal!

103
00:06:54.220 --> 00:06:59.164
Billy Andrews had asked his sister to propose for him, and if Anne wouldn't marry him, he would

104
00:06:59.204 --> 00:07:00.706
ask Nettie Blewett instead.

105
00:07:00.726 --> 00:07:07.871
"Well, that ends my romantic dream," thought Anne sadly, "even if it was a bit girlish."
